      "description": "_rollback_conversation guards the conversation store's missing truncate_messages method but not a call to it that raises. The lookup uses getattr(store, \"truncate_messages\", None) and logs at ERROR when absent, but the call at line 247 is unguarded. Its only caller is the except asyncio.CancelledError handler at lines 427 to 438, so an exception from that call would travel out of the handler and replace the cancellation the bare raise at line 438 propagates, with nothing recording that the rollback did not happen. The shipped BoundedConversationStore raises only ValueError for a negative length and the caller derives baseline_messages from len(...)-or-zero, so the shipped wiring cannot reach this path; an embedder supplying its own store could.",
